    {
        "id": "sea-and-sky_npcc_hitchhiker",
        "name": "Hitchhiker",
        "role": "defender",
        "info": {
            "flavor": "In the early days of the Makaptan labor conflict, logistical issues on both sides limited the number of chassis that could be fielded at once. As a workaround, fighters would train in the perilous art of mech jockeying, enabling them to multiply force at a much lower material cost. Although advances in infrastructure have removed the need for these so-called \"hitchhikers\", a few dauntless individuals continue to swear by the technique's effectiveness.",
            "tactics": "The Hitchhiker clings to an ally to passively augment its own defenses while providing support fire and interfering with nearby enemies' attacks. Its optionals can grant its partner a variety of offensive and defensive buffs. Hitchhikers function best when enabling frontliners and are less durable and effective if isolated."
        },
