    {
        "id": "sea-and-sky_npcc_monsoon",
        "name": "Monsoon",
        "role": "artillery",
        "info": {
            "flavor": "Monsoon-class frames date back to the Maguayan civil war and were first developed by Flue for the defense of Opal's capital city. The archetype's defining characteristics are the use of advanced e-warfare systems to secure a defensive perimeter and bursts of overwhelming firepower to pre-empt approach. Modern incarnations incorporate technology from IPS-N's Raleigh platform to smoothly transition between shielded and firing stances.",
            "tactics": "True to its namesake, the Monsoon alternates between wielding long-range firepower and shielding itself from close-quarters fire. It can protect nearby allies by granting them hard cover and redirecting attacks towards itself. Clever foes will exploit its inability to control when its shields are down, as well as its reliance on offense to handle ranged attackers."
        },
