    {
        "id": "sea-and-sky_npcc_thermostat",
        "name": "Thermostat",
        "role": "controller",
        "info": {
            "flavor": "Advanced climate-control technology, originally developed for life support systems in Makaptan's most extreme environments, is the basis for the Thermostat archetype. Remote-effect liturgicode allows the Thermostat to effectively control other mechs' reactor temperatures in apparent violation of the laws of thermodynamics. Once a rarity outside of the Kahilwayan system, Thermostat chassis are gaining popularity across Union space, much to the chagrin of Harrison Armory designers.",
            "tactics": "Thermostats manipulate Heat – both their own and that of other mechs – to fuel powerful systems. They can punish Danger Zone-abusing enemies by either overloading them with Heat or sapping it away. Thermostats themselves achieve peak performance and durability in the Danger Zone, but peppering them with repeated attacks will force them out."
        },
