    {
        "id": "sea-and-sky_npcc_tunneler",
        "name": "Tunneler",
        "role": "striker",
        "info": {
            "flavor": "The first mechs fielded in the Makaptan labor conflict were repurposed excavators previously used to create space for tunnel boring machines. Today's Tunneler-class frames are the culmination of that technology, boasting full maneuverability underground and independent tunnel-boring capability. However, they come with steep maintenance costs and the tendency to max out cooling systems.",
            "tactics": "Tunnelers dive into the earth to bypass obstacles, then strike from below with increased accuracy. They excel at punching through defensive lines and can leave behind tunnels to allow their allies easy access to objectives. Although tough, Tunnelers are slow aboveground, and they are susceptible to control effects and having their tunnels turned against them."
        },
        "stats": {
